Based on my research, I understand the orientation function computes the sign of the cross product of vectors (q-p) and (r-p). The function should return LEFT_TURN (1), RIGHT_TURN (-1), or COLLINEAR (0).

```cpp
// Compute the orientation using the cross product
// cross = (q.x - p.x) * (r.y - p.y) - (q.y - p.y) * (r.x - p.x)
FT cross = (q.x() - p.x()) * (r.y() - p.y()) - (q.y() - p.y()) * (r.x() - p.x());

if (cross > FT(0)) {
    return CGAL::LEFT_TURN;
} else if (cross < FT(0)) {
    return CGAL::RIGHT_TURN;
} else {
    return CGAL::COLLINEAR;
}
```

